# Chaos: a head and cape layer round the body (O747; client/BASE.md "0210"; src/client/chaoswear.h (new, pure), outfit.cpp, outfit.h,
# creature.cpp, luafunctions_client.cpp; after 0001-0209).
# Owner 2026-11-24: "com levitação e camada nova". The purchased head pieces and capes of pair 83 are creature looks with a back
# (y pattern 0) and a front (y pattern 1). The server's cosmetics say who wears which (kinds head and cape, the "looks" of the
# cosmetics opcode); game_cosmetics hands it in by character name (setCreatureWear, clearCreatureWear). Creature::draw gives the
# outfit the pieces of a player (a widget's preview creature, id 0, and a player in a list too) and Outfit::draw draws the cape's
# and the head piece's backs before the body and their fronts after it, each by its anchor tile of chaospiece.h (0209) on the
# wearer's tile, lifted with the body, in its own looping frame. Never on a mount; a piece without a chaospiece.h row, or a pair
# without the look, is not drawn. Nothing changes for a character that wears neither.
diff -ruN a/src/client/chaoswear.h b/src/client/chaoswear.h
